  "title": "review: fix round 1 for T-1508: mirror the CLAUDE.md delegation wording into .orchestrator/prompts/planner.md so the prompt-parity test passes",
  "spec": "Fix round for T-1508 (goal T-1403, B3), branch cut from task/T-1508 (commit 8e0773a added mcp.execute, the codex/codex_reply refusal, executor_fallback Claude rows, the catalog/allowlist entries and rewrote CLAUDE.md lines 4 and 8). The focused tests passed (32/32) but the full gate failed one test outside the task's focused set with:\n\nAssertionError: '- Ed[25 chars] via `codex` / `codex_reply`; Codex cooling \u2192 [631 chars].md.' != '- Ed[25 chars] via the execute tool (any enabled executor ro[704 chars].md.'\n\nThe expected text is the OLD 'Never' line, which still lives in .orchestrator/prompts/planner.md line 4 (the headless Planner system prompt; `f orch` and planner-prompt.sh repeat CLAUDE.md's rules from it); the actual text is the new CLAUDE.md line 8. A test asserts the two files agree. Fix: apply exactly the same wording change to .orchestrator/prompts/planner.md (both the Roles sentence and the 'Never: Edit source files' bullet) that T-1508 applied to CLAUDE.md lines 4 and 8, so the two files agree line for line again. Run `.claude/hooks/tests-green.sh .` once to find the failing test id, name it in the result, and make it pass without editing that test. If the parity test compares other lines that T-1508 changed, mirror those too; change nothing else in either file.\n\nCommit first, then run the test file that holds the parity test plus tests/test_mcp.py in the foreground; never background a command.",
  "inputs": [
    "T-1527"
  ],
  "acceptance": [
    "the prompt-parity test that failed the T-1508 gate (named in the result) passes with CLAUDE.md and .orchestrator/prompts/planner.md carrying the same delegation wording",
