  "result": {
    "summary": "The 'Never: Edit source files' bullet in .orchestrator/prompts/planner.md is now byte-identical to CLAUDE.md. tests/test_goals.py::PlannerPromptAndConfig::test_planner_md_matches_claude_md_lists compares the first line, the Never section and the Always section, so that is the parity test the fix targets. The Roles sentence exists only in CLAUDE.md. planner.md has no Roles line, so there is nothing to mirror there. The visible mcp.py hunks look sound: `codex` refuses with a clear status when no codex row is enabled, and `execute` posts its result the same way `codex` does. I did not run the tests. The diff was truncated, and this worktree (T-1532) is not on the reviewed branch, so I could not see the remaining 79 lines. That includes the `codex_reply` refusal, the rest of the mcp.py changes, and the body of test_execute_tool_dispatches_and_codex_tools_refuse_without_codex_row. This verdict covers only the visible hunks.",
